// A playing card in a standard deck.
// On the page each card is its own element, `<solitaire-card>`
a "card" is a draggable two sided view
	its "rank" is one of ace, 2 ... 10, jack, queen, king
		it "is a (rank)"
	it "is a face card" if its rank is jack, queen or king

	its "suit" is one of clubs, diamonds, hearts or spades
		it "is a (suit)"
	it "is the (rank) of (suit)"

	its "color" is one of red, black
		red if it is a diamond or it is a heart
		black otherwise
	its "symbol" is
		"♣" if it is a club
		"♦" if it is a diamond
		"♥" if it is a heart
		"♠" otherwise

	its "direction" is one of down, up
		it "is face (direction)"
	to turn a card face up: set its direction to up
	to turn it face down: set its direction to down
	to turn it over
		if it is face down: turn it face up
		otherwise turn it face down

	to test card properties
		get a new card whose rank is queen, suit is spades and direction is down
		its color should be black
		it is a face card should be yes
		it is the queen of spades should be yes
		its direction should be down
		turn it over
		its direction should be up
